WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
If your prep is SuTab, this video will walk you through exactly how to take it.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Just follow along step by step.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.310
Your SuTab kit includes two bottles of 12 tablets each and a measured

4
00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:09.840
container.

5
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:14.320
Start your first dose between 6 and 7 PM the night before your procedure.

6
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.720
Open your first bottle of 12 tablets.

7
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:21.760
Fill the provided container with 16 ounces of water up to the fill line.

8
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:25.200
Swallow one tablet every 2 minutes with a sip of water, finishing all 12

9
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:25.760
tablets over

10
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:29.280
about 15 to 20 minutes. Take your time and go at a steady pace.

11
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.250
About 1 hour after your last tablet, fill the container again with 16 ounces

12
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:34.800
of water

13
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.600
and drink the entire amount slowly over 30 minutes.

14
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.850
Then about 30 minutes after finishing that container, fill it one more time

15
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:41.680
with 16 ounces

16
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.740
of water and drink the entire amount over 30 minutes. That completes your first

17
00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:46.000
dose.

18
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.360
7 hours prior to your procedure, repeat the exact same three steps

19
00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.360
using your second bottle of 12 tablets. One tablet every 2 minutes with water,

20
00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:59.390
then 16 ounces of water one hour later, then 16 ounces of water 30 minutes

21
00:00:59.390 --> 00:00:59.840
after that.

22
00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.900
This part is really important. You must drink all of the prep solution as

23
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:04.640
directed,

24
00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.480
even if you're already passing clear liquid.

25
00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:10.690
I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the entire dose is what gives us

26
00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:11.520
the clearest

27
00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.280
view during your procedure. If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may

28
00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:16.400
need to reschedule,

29
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.540
and neither of us wants that. Between doses, keep drinking clear liquids to

30
00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:21.200
stay hydrated,

31
00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.680
it will help you feel better and help the prep do its job.

32
00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:28.220
Do not drink anything at all within 4 hours of your procedure, including

33
00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:28.800
water,

34
00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.970
unless it is a small sip to take a medication. Your procedure may be canceled

35
00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:33.680
or rescheduled

36
00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.760
if this is not followed. If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips

37
00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:38.640
to the bathroom,

38
00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:42.160
applying a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

39
00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:48.640
That's it. You've got this. Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay

40
00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:49.520
hydrated.

41
00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:53.310
If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office. We're here

42
00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:54.000
to help.
